## Phased Implementation Roadmap

### Phase 1: Foundation & Workspace Setup
- Initialize root `package.json`, `pnpm-workspace.yaml`, and `turbo.json`.
- Configure `docker-compose.yml` with PostgreSQL 16, Redis 7, and Mailpit (for local email capture).
- Create `packages/config` (TS, ESLint, Prettier), `packages/types`, and `packages/database`.
- Define comprehensive Prisma schema and verify migration generation.
- Scaffold `apps/api` (NestJS), `apps/workers` (NestJS + BullMQ), `apps/storefront` (Next.js), and `apps/admin` (Next.js).

### Phase 2: Authentication & Authorization (RBAC)
- Customer registration, login, refresh token rotation, logout.
- HTTP-only secure cookie management.
- Admin authentication with role-based access control (`SUPER_ADMIN`, `MERCHANDISER`, `FULFILLMENT_STAFF`).
- Password reset flow with secure token hashing.

### Phase 3: Catalog & Search Modules
- Product & Variant CRUD with multi-attribute matrix generation (Color x Size).
- Category tree & curated collection endpoints.
- High-performance PostgreSQL Full-Text Search with GIN index on text fields + facet aggregations.
- Media upload service integration with DigitalOcean Spaces S3 adapter and URL generation.

### Phase 4: Inventory & Stock Reservation
- Atomic reservation mechanism using PostgreSQL `$transaction` and row locks:
  - Check `quantityOnHand - reservedQuantity >= requestedQuantity`.
  - Create `InventoryReservation` with 15-minute TTL.
- Automatic release on cart item removal or cancellation.

### Phase 5: Cart & Promotions
- Persistent guest carts and logged-in user cart synchronization.
- Coupon engine supporting percentage discounts, flat discounts, minimum order thresholds, and usage limits.
- Dynamic cart subtotal, tax, shipping, and promotional discount recalculation.

### Phase 6: Checkout, Orders & Payment Gateway
- Checkout state machine: Address selection -> Reservation verification -> Payment initiation.
- Payment adapter integration: Razorpay & Cashfree test mode + signature verification + idempotent webhook handlers.
- Order creation transaction: Converts cart to order, marks reservations as fulfilled, updates permanent inventory.
- Refund handling logic.

### Phase 7: Background Worker System (BullMQ)
- Worker module consuming Redis queues:
  - `email.send`: Order confirmation, shipping updates, password resets (via Nodemailer / Mailpit / SendGrid / SES).
  - `invoice.generate`: Automated PDF invoice generation and storage in Spaces.
  - `inventory.cleanup`: Scheduled job (every 2 minutes) to release expired checkout reservations.
  - `notification.send`: Customer SMS/WhatsApp alerts.

### Phase 8: Luxury Next.js Storefront
- High-end editorial aesthetic:
  - Curated typography (Cinzel / Playfair Display / Cormorant + Inter).
  - Editorial campaign hero banner with luxury video/imagery.
  - Curated collection lookbooks ("Handcrafted Silk", "Atelier Noir", "Autumn Cashmere").
- Core customer journeys:
  - PLP with instant faceted filtering (Size, Color, Fabric, Price, Sort).
  - PDP with high-resolution image zoom, interactive size selector with real-time stock indicator, accordion specs, styling suggestions.
  - Smooth slide-over cart drawer with real-time promo code feedback.
  - Streamlined 2-step luxury checkout.
  - Customer account hub with order tracking timeline.

### Phase 9: Next.js Admin Portal
- Executive KPI overview: Today's GMV, Orders, Average Order Value, Low Stock Alerts.
- Product matrix builder: Add products, generate variants, manage inventory per SKU, upload gallery photos.
- Order fulfillment console: View incoming orders, inspect line items, advance status (`PROCESSING` -> `SHIPPED`), assign tracking numbers.
- Coupon & campaign manager.

### Phase 10: Production Docker & Deployment Configuration
- Multi-stage `Dockerfile` for `api`, `workers`, `storefront`, and `admin`.
- Production `docker-compose.prod.yml` configured for a single DigitalOcean Droplet with reverse proxy.
- GitHub Actions CI workflow (lint, type-check, automated tests, Docker build).
- Cloudflare Free setup guide for DNS, SSL, and caching rules.

